  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Les Trévires trains its members at the Stade du Camp Marin, with a broad range of dog disciplines: obedience, ring, mondioring, water work and rescue.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>An important point to check before heading over: our research identified a club called "Éducation Canine du Golfe de Grimaud", based at the place called Les Trévires in Plan-de-la-Tour, with a training ground at Stade du Camp Marin located in Grimaud (not Sainte-Maxime) — chaired by Mrs Véronique Porcu (04 94 55 54 86 / 06 80 65 36 74), practising mondioring and obedience. A neighbouring club at the same place name ("Club d'Éducation Canine Plantourian") practises a list of disciplines closer to the one shown here (ring, obedience, mondioring, field work, tracking, utility search), but still without the "rescue" mention. It's possible that this listing conflates two clubs based at the same place name, in a different commune from the one stated. As with any club run by volunteers, get in touch before heading over — all the more essential here to confirm the exact name and commune.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if your dog has energy to spare, a multi-discipline club like this one is a good way to channel that energy during an extended stay in the area.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Sainte-Maxime and its town centre are close to the Stade du Camp Marin.</p>
